MOBILE BEFORE/AFTER CAPTURES — SHIPPED (controller run 146, 2026-11-22,
same board card, after run 145 died at the cap):
- before/: 3/3 PASS — dictation_target serves «Я учу́ ру́сский язы́к.» to a
  zero-encounter profile (complaint reproduced), hub offers Speaking, the
  sentence is visibly rendered (speaking-before.png).
- after/: 3/3 PASS — dictation_target REFUSES (422, "no sentence practice
  is unlocked yet — finish more lessons to unlock it"), practice_queue is
  34 entries ALL kind=orthography (the 34 merged letter entities), the
  speaking screen shows no sentence (speaking-after.png).
- practice-hub-before/after.png are byte-identical by design: the hub is
  unchanged by this lane; the visual delta is entirely on the speaking
  screen. Vision-checked both speaking shots.
- Harness fixes that made it work (scripts/practice-gate-capture.mjs):
  1) node V8 OOM: readFileSync(300MB lpk).toString('base64') +
     JSON.stringify ~ 1.5GB of V8 strings (run 145's core-dump 134).
  2) base64-over-HTTP import is a dead end ANYWAY: axum's DefaultBodyLimit
     (2MB) 413s any real pack — production never imports via HTTP
     (catalog installs download server-side). Fix: seed via serve's OWN
     install_pack command, which builds+installs the archive in-process
     from the dev tree baked into that binary at compile time — so
     lts-serve-before installs the pre-lane tree (c431333 worktree with
     hardlinked gitignored media) and lts-serve-after the committed tree.
  3) SERVE_DIST is the dist DIRECTORY (serve joins index.html itself);
     run 145's 'pass index.html' note was the script's own readFileSync
     EISDIR trap.
  4) chooser card buttons read 'Continue' — profile name lives in the card
     wrapper (MOBILE-UX-001 lesson), match the container.
  5) CDP: Page.enable after attach, and Page.captureScreenshot must carry
     the sessionId (browser session has no Page domain).
- NEW follow-up surfaced by the after shot (NOT fixed here): the frontend
  Speaking screen shows a silently-empty input when the engine refuses;
  the honest refusal TEXT exists engine-side but no empty-state copy
  renders in the UI. Frontend UX follow-up, same family as the deferred
